{
  "_README": "Measured per-package vitest wall time (seconds), used ONLY to balance the CI test shards in .github/workflows/test.yml. Nothing gates on these numbers: an entry that is stale, missing, or wrong costs a slightly lopsided shard and nothing else. To regenerate after the suite has drifted, run this script with --record once per shard log. Record ALL SIX shards of one green run: measurements merge OVER the existing table, never replacing it, because one log only covers that shard's packages.  for N in 1 2 3 4 5 6; do JID=$(gh api \"repos/MemberJunction/MJ/actions/runs/<runId>/jobs?per_page=100\" --jq \".jobs[]|select(.name==\\\"Unit tests (shard $N/6)\\\")|.id\"); gh run view --repo MemberJunction/MJ --job \"$JID\" --log | perl -pe 's/\\Q^[\\E/\\x1b/g' > shard$N.log; node .github/scripts/plan-test-shards.mjs --record=shard$N.log --source=\"run <runId> shard $N/6\"; done.  TWO TRAPS: the `gh api .../jobs/<id>/logs` form documented previously returns 0 bytes; and `gh run view --log` escapes ESC as the two literal characters ^[, which defeats this script's ANSI strip so it finds no durations and records nothing while still printing a success-looking message. The perl filter turns them back into real escapes; without it the whole regeneration is a silent no-op.",
